{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>Then</b> [באדין], <b>prostrated</b> [סגיד] — he bowed down and prostrated himself to him and worshipped." "<b>Aroma</b> [ניחוחין] — now, he considered him like a deity."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes the Aramaic words from the verse and then renders them into Hebrew; the Hebrew translation is itself a chain of near-synonyms.", 1 "The verse word ניחוחין literally means 'sweet savour/aroma'; the comment addresses why the king offered incense or oblation to Daniel, implying he treated him as divine."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:25.132945616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}